message: "If you use this evaluation, its dataset, or its code, please cite it as below."
title: "Triage Under Pressure (TUP): a multi-turn evaluation of whether LLM medical advisors maintain emergency-care recommendations under disclosed barriers to care"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ramanan
    given-names: Rasika
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-17
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/rasikaramanan/triage-under-pressure"
url: "https://rasikaramanan.github.io/triage-under-pressure/"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - LLM evaluation
  - AI safety
  - medical triage
  - health equity
  - multi-turn dialogue
  - sycophancy
abstract: >-
  TUP tests whether LLM medical advisors that give a correct emergency-care
  recommendation maintain it across a multi-turn conversation after the user
  discloses a barrier to seeking care (cost, no insurance, transport, work,
  caregiving), against a cooperative control and a non-structural comparator
  (fear of hospitals).
  1,960 conversations across 14 externally-sourced emergency vignettes, seven
  conditions, and five frontier advisor models, scored by a three-judge panel
  against a fixed clinician-vetted gold standard, with the full instrument
  prespecified in an executable lock and every transcript released.
